Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:34:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the sender and order filters alive across a stepping
 jump
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two search branches each grew their own way to revive a search session after
RoomView is re-mounted for another room, and the merge kept both. The
constructor seeds the full render state; componentDidMount then re-seeded it
from a hand-written object literal that predates the sender filter, the result
order and the match list, so whichever ran last decided what survived — and
componentDidMount runs last.

The visible cost was a stepping jump quietly resetting the from: chip and the
relevance toggle, and a match counter with nothing to count. Deferring to the
same builder the constructor uses removes the second, older answer rather than
patching fields into it, so a field added to the session cannot go missing here
again.
---
 apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.tsx | 16 +---------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.tsx
index 5a8c2953b0..5c8f4dd283 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/structures/RoomView.tsx
@@ -2112,21 +2112,7 @@ export class RoomView extends React.Component<IRoomProps, IRoomState> {
         const session = SearchSessionStore.instance.getSnapshot();
         if (!session || SearchSessionStore.instance.focusedMatch === null) return;
 
-        this.setState({
-            search: {
-                searchId: session.searchId,
-                roomId: session.roomId,
-                term: session.term,
-                scope: session.scope,
-                promise: session.promise,
-                abortController: session.abortController,
-                inProgress: session.inProgress,
-                count: session.count,
-                error: session.error,
-                currentMatchIndex: session.currentMatchIndex,
-                highlights: session.highlights,
-            },
-        });
+        this.setState({ search: searchInfoFromSession(session) });
     }
 
     /**
